    "TaskTransitionOutcome": {
      "action": "add",
      "docs": "Result of transition_task: the transition happened, or it was refused with the typed reason. Type-design: an admission refusal is a legitimate result rather than an exceptional condition, so it travels as data and keeps its scope, contribution, ceiling and batch payloads intact — the same outcome-as-data shape the Phase 3 gate uses for BatchPlanGateOutcome, instead of collapsing to a rendered string in the error channel. This also leaves TaskOperationError's declared shape identical to its baseline. Role Dto in usecase (R1 △, justification): it is the output carrier of the pre-existing TaskOperationOutput DTO in this same module, crossing the usecase-to-driver boundary; it is not identified by value equality, so ValueObject would be the wrong classification. IN-09, IN-10, AC-10, AC-12.",
